{
  "id": "bulk-cards-all-actions-local",
  "title": "bulkCards add_tags, remove_tags, set_preset, move and delete are answered on the device (C-31)",
  "covers": [
    "cards.bulk_all_actions_local"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Three kana-only words (cards 1-3), two user decks (Inbox holds note 1), one extra preset. Before C-31 the shell forwarded every action used here.",
    "Steps 0-1: dry_run reports what would happen and changes nothing.",
    "Steps 2-4: add_tags tags both notes (one note.updated each); repeating it changes nothing and counts both in skipped (no op).",
    "Steps 5-7: remove_tags on card 1 only.",
    "Steps 8-9: set_preset (one card.preset_set per card).",
    "Steps 10-12: move puts both notes into Later (deck.item_put each) and removes note 1 from Inbox (one deck.item_removed; note 2 was not in it). ops_emitted is left to the golden.",
    "Steps 13-14: delete by query (tag:later matches card 2 only) emits one card.deleted; the card answers 410.",
    "Step 15: delete of an already deleted card is skipped; card 3 is deleted.",
    "Step 16: only card 1 is left in the card list.",
    "The shell mints every op as the device, in one transaction per call; op-level tests (schema validity, idempotency, out-of-order convergence) are LF-A5's, not parity's."
  ],
